vendor/kanjidic/kanji-readings.json holds the on'yomi and kun'yomi of the
kanji in KANJIDIC2. Hachidori uses them to place headword furigana over the
kanji each reading belongs to.

This package uses the KANJIDIC2 dictionary file. This file is the property of
the Electronic Dictionary Research and Development Group, and is used in
conformance with the Group's licence:

  Licence: https://www.edrdg.org/edrdg/licence.html
  KANJIDIC project: https://www.edrdg.org/wiki/index.php/KANJIDIC_Project

Copyright over KANJIDIC2 is held by James William Breen and the Electronic
Dictionary Research and Development Group.

The readings were taken from KANJIDIC_english.zip of yomidevs/jmdict-yomitan;
vendor/kanjidic/source.json records its URL, SHA-256 and KANJIDIC revision.
Changes: only the readings are kept, all in hiragana; a kun'yomi keeps the "."
before its okurigana; the "-" that marks a prefix or suffix reading is
removed; a repeated reading is listed once; kanji without readings are left
out.

